TUnit uses `[Before(...)]` and `[After(...)]` attributes with a `HookType` enum to control scope. Here's each level:

## 1. Before/After Every Test (method-level)

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public void ResetDatabase(TestContext context)
    {
        InMemoryDb.Reset();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public void Cleanup(TestContext context) { /* ... */ }

    [Test]
    public async Task Order_IsCreated() { /* ... */ }
}
```

## 2. Before First / After Last Test in a Class (class-level)

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    private static HttpClient _client;

    [Before(Class)]
    public static void OpenFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        _client = new HttpClient();
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static void DisposeFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        _client.Dispose();
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Order_IsCreated() { /* ... */ }
}
```

## 3. Before/After All Tests in an Assembly

```csharp
public class WireMockSetup
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static void StartServer(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        WireMockServer.Start();
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static void StopServer(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        WireMockServer.Stop();
    }
}
```

## 4. Once Per Entire Test Session (global)

```csharp
public class GlobalSetup
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static void ApplyMigrations(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        Database.Migrate();
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static void TearDown(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        Database.Drop();
    }
}
```

## Summary

| Scope | Attribute | Method must be | Context parameter |
|-------|-----------|---------------|-------------------|
| Each test | `[Before(Test)]` / `[After(Test)]` | Instance | `TestContext` |
| Class | `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` | `static` | `ClassHookContext` |
| Assembly | `[Before(Assembly)]` / `[After(Assembly)]` | `static` | `AssemblyHookContext` |
| Session | `[Before(TestSession)]` / `[After(TestSession)]` | `static` | `TestSessionContext` |

The `HookType` values (`Test`, `Class`, `Assembly`, `TestSession`) are statically imported from `TUnit.Core.HookType`. Class/Assembly/Session hooks can live in any class — TUnit discovers them by attribute. All hooks support `async Task` return types as well.
